      "value": "yes",
      "items": [
        "SH2-R1"
      ],
      "basis": "The Billing API and retry record could have resolved whether authoritative API state was eventually recovered or whether the snapshot fallback remained effective authority, which remained an explicit uncertainty in the initial response. SH2-R4 was potentially confirmatory for the test-case gap, but the settlement surface already stated the fixture and test situation, so it is less clearly decisive."
    },
    "decisive_item_located": {
      "value": "partly yes",
      "basis": "SH2-R2 and SH2-R3 located decisive confirmations of the two D_now+ defects: unverified stale snapshot use and the collapsing helper definition. SH2-R1 could have been decisive for the remaining API-recovery uncertainty but was not selected."
    },
    "index_induced_new_reasoning": {
      "value": "no",
      "basis": "Both the authority/freshness substitution and identity/helper concerns were present in the initial free-text response before selection; the index labels align with, rather than create, those concerns."
    },
    "post_audit_action_confidence_change_appropriate": {
      "value": "appropriate",
      "basis": "After SH2-R2 and SH2-R3 returned, the recipient kept request-repair, lowered confidence slightly from 5/100 to 3/100, kept acceptance evidence insufficient, and added precise uncertainty; this is proportional because the retrieved artifacts confirmed but did not substantially worsen an already low-confidence defect set."
    }
  },
